pkgrm(8)										   pkgrm(8)

NAME
     pkgrm - remove software package

SYNOPSIS
     pkgrm [options] <package>

DESCRIPTION
     pkgrm  is	a package management utility, which removes/uninstalls a previously installed soft‐
     ware packages.

OPTIONS
     -r, --root <path>
	    Specify alternative installation root (default is "/"). This should be used if you want
	    to remove a package from a temporary mounted partition, which  is  "owned"	by  another
	    system.  By using this option you not only specify where the software is installed, but
	    you also specify which package database to use.

     -v, --version
	    Print version and exit.

     -h, --help
	    Print help and exit.

SEE ALSO
     pkgadd(8), pkginfo(8), pkgmk(8), rejmerge(8)

